General characteristics — Full bore, Battery / Renewable energy powered\" similarly.\n\n- characteristics.config_level: axis \"power_supply\", attribute q1..q4, ratio_q3_q1 with values being arrays per condition? The schema says config_level entries: {attribute, axis, values: [{condition, value, unit_symbol}]}. But each condition would have many values (per meter size & class) — that doesn't fit since value must be a single structured value. So config_level isn't ideal for the full matrix. Better to keep the tables in matrix_tables and possibly extract model_level for the base? But flow rates vary by both size AND power config.\n\nI think the best representation:\n- matrix_tables with the two tables fully captured.\n- model_family.models: list of DN sizes.\n- Possibly characteristics.model_level for q3 across models? But q3 also depends on power config and class. For AC mains: Q3 depends only on size (40, 63, 100, 160, 250, 250, 630, 1000, 1600, 2500, 4000, 4000, 6300, 6300, 6300, 10000, 10000, 10000, 10000, 10000, 10000, 10000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000). For battery: Q3 same per size actually (40, 63, 100, 160, 250, 250, 630, 1000, 1600, 2500, 4000, 4000, 6300, 6300, 6300, 10000, 10000, 10000, 10000, 10000, 10000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000, 16000). Wait battery table lacks DN650? Let me check: battery table covers DN40, DN50, DN65, DN80, DN100, DN125, DN150, DN200, DN250, DN300, DN350, DN400, DN450, DN500, DN600, DN700, DN750, DN800, DN900 (class 2 only), DN1000 (2), DN1050 (2), DN1100 (2), DN1200 (2), DN1350 (2), DN1400 (2), DN1500 (2), DN1600 (2), DN1650 (2). No DN1800 in battery. Q3 values match the AC values per size.\n\nRather than overcomplicate, I'll:\n- Put both tables in matrix_tables (complete).\n- Add model_level characteristics for q1, q2, q3, q4 and ratio_q3_q1? That would be a huge duplication and ambiguous wrt config. The schema says matrix_tables is for \"preserve multi-dim tables tha